{"id":"f41ee283-e768-4af9-9f85-b376da65e6ab","kind":"note","ref":{"span":"a188819edeb28fbc","key":"bablr1","file":"packages/editor/workbench/terminal/invoke.ts","baseline":{"blob":"fdd522e54a7aeb14ee5c2ca027ae04dfad8b3073","start":0,"end":76},"shape":{"type":"ImportDeclaration","atoms":["import","type","{","JuvyCommand",",","RunProcess","}","from","\"","@brianjenkins94/util/juvy/cli","\""]},"context":{"after":"eb43e5d923caaa07"}},"payload":{"text":"A command's definition (command.ts) and implementation as a just-bash command, run through juvy: juvy routes its\nsubcommands, parses its options and arguments by its schema (strictly — an unknown flag is an error, as it is in a real\nCLI), validates them, renders `--help` and \"did you mean\", and hands the parsed config to the handler. juvy's `run`\nwrites to and exits through the process it's given — here, one that collects the command's output — so the same juvy\nthat runs a desktop CLI (packages/silo) runs the terminal's commands.\n\nKept out of catalog.ts (which only Vite can read, for its glob), so a command's test can make its command here.","wrote":["Brian Jenkins"]},"author":"local","createdAt":"2026-11-22T18:07:54.258Z","updatedAt":"2026-11-22T18:07:54.258Z"}
